          "type": "output_text",
          "annotations": [],
          "logprobs": [],
          "text": "{\"occurrence_id\":\"tolstoy-war-and-peace-8dd4aaa6bea98c65\",\"core_classification\":{\"label_support\":{\"truth_conditional\":4,\"performative\":0,\"exclamatory_reflexive\":0,\"other\":0},\"confidence\":0.97,\"analysis\":\"Prince Andrei directly avows his love for Pierre as the reason he trusts him with an intimate, unprecedented confession. The utterance presents an existing state of affectionate friendship as true. It does not itself undertake a commitment, and its deliberate placement in a causal clause provides no independent evidence of expressive/reflexive discharge.\",\"ambiguity\":\"The avowal helps affirm their intimate bond, but that relational effect does not amount to performative undertaking force.\"},\"other_diagnosis\":{\"tpe_failure\":null,\"core_not_context\":null},\"utterance_status\":{\"status\":\"direct\",\"description\":\"Prince Andrei addresses Pierre directly; the core words occur in the causal clause «потому что я люблю тебя» (“because I love you”) within his spoken explanation.\"},\"contextual_interpretation\":\"Andrei invokes his love for Pierre to explain why Pierre alone is the first person entrusted with his deeply private unhappiness about marriage. The declaration expresses close, confidential friendship and licenses unusual candour. Although Andrei is nervously animated, the words are integrated into a deliberate explanation rather than presented as an involuntary emotional outburst.\",\"evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"e1\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"«Это я тебе одному и первому говорю, потому что я люблю тебя» (“I am telling you this alone, and you are the first person I have told, because I love you”).\",\"supports\":\"Strong truth-conditional force: Andrei presents his love for Pierre as an existing fact that explains exclusive trust and disclosure.\",\"confidence\":0.99},{\"evidence_id\":\"e2\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"The narration compares Andrei to someone who has long had something on his mind and suddenly resolves to speak out.\",\"supports\":\"The conversation is a deliberate act of disclosure; this weighs against treating the love clause as reflex-like verbal discharge.\",\"confidence\":0.96},{\"evidence_id\":\"e3\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"After the avowal, Andrei continues: «Ты не понимаешь, отчего я это говорю» (“You do not understand why I am saying this”).\",\"supports\":\"The love utterance functions within an explanation of why Andrei confides in Pierre, reinforcing assertive/avowal force rather than commitment force.\",\"confidence\":0.96},{\"evidence_id\":\"e4\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"Andrei’s face quivers with nervous animation and his eyes shine brightly while he speaks.\",\"supports\":\"The delivery is emotionally intense, but the passage supplies intensity rather than independent evidence that the love words themselves are an expressive/reflexive discharge.\",\"confidence\":0.93},{\"evidence_id\":\"e5\",\"source\":\"supplied_metadata\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"The occurrence is marked as affirmative present tense in a main-or-embedded construction and reviewed as a valid explicit “I love you” instance.\",\"supports\":\"Corroborates identification of the embedded affirmative love avowal as the core event.\",\"confidence\":0.98}],\"background_knowledge\":{\"used\":false,\"familiarity\":\"none\",\"confidence\":null,\"contribution\":null},\"ontology_assessment\":{\"fit\":\"natural\",\"diagnosis\":\"T naturally captures the core avowal. Its confidential function and emotional delivery are adequately represented as context and do not require P, E, or O.\",\"candidate_recurrent_dimension\":null},\"notes\":null}"
        }
